From 5fe0e7daff48bde9b837333c41e1d16a62f3b88a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mir Mohammad Sajedul Islam <mohammad.sajedul.islam@g.bracu.ac.bd>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:57:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dashboard): interactive student dashboard with synced
 progress

Student dashboard
- Redesign to match the landing page: ambient sky/ember backdrop, glowing
  colour-cycling nav icons, ember call-to-action buttons, sliding nav pills
- Home: greeting, "continue where you left off" card, real study streak with a
  7-day strip, weekly goal ring, course coverage ring, subject launchpads with
  progress, due-today and up-next lists, practice lab, badges, XP and levels
- Lectures: chapter progress rings, tap-to-load video (thumbnail first),
  YouTube player that resumes at the last position and completes a lecture at
  90%, timestamped notes that autosave, "Ask AI" shortcuts that send the
  chapter or lecture to the tutor
- Simulations inside chapters: a matching simulation is suggested on each
  chapter page (English and Bangla chapter names)
- Auto revision: finishing a lecture adds reminders 1, 3 and 7 days later
- Notice bell opens the full notice; unread dot instead of a permanent ping
- Celebration toast with confetti for chapters, badges and level-ups
- Search now covers study sheets as well as lectures; PDF preview is a sheet
- Back button works: view, subject, chapter and lecture live in the URL

Removed
- Fake "Igniting Catalyst" loading screen and hard-coded "Streak Active" badge
- History trap that blocked the Back button
- 600 ms blocking overlay on every subject switch

Reliability
- Dashboard uses the shared API client (timeout and retry) and shows the last
  saved lectures while the server wakes up, with a clear retry message
- Progress is saved on the phone first and queued when offline, then synced
- Existing browser-only progress, notes and plans are imported once

Backend
- New progress API: lecture progress, notes, study plans, activity days and a
  one-time import, with tables created at startup
- Tests for the progress API (backend/tests)
